examples.question_text:
Use a protractor to construct a $45^{\circ}$ angle anticlockwise from the base arm.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(4,0);
\fill (0,0) circle (1.5pt);
\path (0,0) node[below] {$V$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
Place the protractor centre on $V$ and align its zero line with the base arm. Follow the scale starting at zero on the right. Mark $45^{\circ}$ anticlockwise, then use a ruler to draw the second arm from $V$ through the mark.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (-2.5,0)--(2.5,0);
\draw (2.5,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=180,radius=2.5];
\foreach \a in {0,10,...,180}{\draw (\a:2.3)--(\a:2.5);}
\foreach \a in {0,30,60,90,120,150,180}{\path (\a:2.05) node {$\a$};}
\draw[thick] (4,0)--(0,0)--(45:4);
\fill (45:2.5) circle (2pt);
\draw (0.8,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=45,radius=0.8];
\path (22.5:1.25) node {$45^{\circ}$};
\path (0,0) node[below] {$V$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The angle is acute because it is less than $90^{\circ}$.

examples.question_text:
The base arm is tilted. Construct an $80^{\circ}$ angle clockwise from it.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(25:4);
\fill (0,0) circle (1.5pt);
\path (0,0) node[left] {$V$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
Centre the protractor on $V$. Rotate it so its zero line follows the tilted base arm, with its curved edge on the clockwise side. Mark $80^{\circ}$ clockwise from the base arm, then rule the second arm from $V$ through the mark.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[thick] (25:4)--(0,0)--(-55:4);
\fill (-55:2.5) circle (2pt);
\draw[->] (25:0.9) arc[start angle=25,end angle=-55,radius=0.9];
\path (-15:1.4) node {$80^{\circ}$};
\path (0,0) node[left] {$V$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Check the turn from the base arm to the second arm, rather than from a horizontal line.

Use the scale whose zero lies along the base arm on the right. Follow that scale to $135$, mark the point and rule the second arm from the vertex through it. The paired $45$ reading belongs to the scale starting at the opposite end.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[thick] (4,0)--(0,0)--(135:4);
\draw (0.9,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=135,radius=0.9];
\path (67.5:1.4) node {$135^{\circ}$};
\path (0,0) node[below] {$V$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The completed angle is obtuse: it is greater than $90^{\circ}$ and less than $180^{\circ}$.

Find the smaller angle:
$\begin{aligned}&\mathrel{\phantom{=}}360^{\circ}-250^{\circ}\\&=110^{\circ}\end{aligned}$
Draw a base arm. Centre the protractor at its endpoint, align zero with the base arm and mark $110^{\circ}$. Rule the second arm through the mark. Label the outside turn $250^{\circ}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[thick] (4,0)--(0,0)--(110:4);
\draw (0.7,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=110,radius=0.7];
\path (55:1.15) node {$110^{\circ}$};
\draw[->] (1.5,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=-250,radius=1.5];
\path (-100:2) node {$250^{\circ}$};
\path (0,0) node[below left] {$V$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.question_text:
A learner correctly marks a point $P$ at $60^{\circ}$ from the base arm, but draws the second arm from $W$ instead of $V$. Explain the error and how to correct it.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (V) at (0,0);
\coordinate (W) at (0.8,0);
\coordinate (P) at (60:3);
\draw (V)--(4,0);
\draw (W)--(P);
\fill (V) circle (1.5pt);
\fill (W) circle (1.5pt);
\fill (P) circle (2pt);
\path (V) node[below] {$V$};
\path (W) node[below] {$W$};
\path (P) node[above] {$P$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
The second arm starts at the wrong point. Both arms must start at $V$. Erase the arm from $W$ and rule the second arm from $V$ through $P$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[thick] (4,0)--(0,0)--(60:4);
\fill (60:3) circle (2pt);
\draw (0.8,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=60,radius=0.8];
\path (30:1.35) node {$60^{\circ}$};
\path (0,0) node[below] {$V$};
\path (60:3) node[above left] {$P$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
